# Hawk V-Lite style 110mm 2x
#
# Front anamorphic made by lenses/make_anamorphic.py from
#   lens_files/Leica_100mm_(Leica_Summilux_C_100mm_T1.4).lens (scaled to 110mm)
# scaled to 110mm, with the iris set to f/3 (the stop of the reference footage).
# A Galilean cylindrical attachment (BK7 glass, coating 0) in front of the
# original lens.  Horizontal field 2x wider (squeeze 2x paraxial), vertical
# unchanged; focal_length below is the vertical (taking lens) focal length.
# The attachment's apertures are 1.5x make_anamorphic.py's default so
# off-axis ghosts are not clipped.
# NOT a Vantage Hawk prescription (none is public).  A stand-in for flare
# work, tuned against Hawk V-Lite test footage: bright full-width white-blue
# streak, magenta veil, soft blue ghost below the light.
# See looks/Hawk_VLite_Style_110mm_2x.json for the matching look.

name: Hawk V-Lite style 110mm 2x
focal_length: 110

surfaces:
# radius     thickness   ior      abbe   semi_ap   coating  type
# --- Front anamorphic attachment: 2x squeeze, cylinder axes vertical ---
  -117.830  3.000  1.51680  64.2  114.4650  0  cyl_y   # plano-concave cylinder, F = -228
  0  211.076  1.00000  0.0  114.4650  0   # flat back, air gap (solved: afocal)
  0  22.670  1.51680  64.2  143.0700  0   # flat front of the positive cylinder
  -235.661  15.000  1.00000  0.0  143.0700  0  cyl_y   # plano-convex cylinder, F = +456
